<% content_for :title, "Connect via SMART on FHIR - Medride" %>

<h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight mb-8">Connect via SMART on FHIR</h1>

<section class="mb-8">
  <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold text-faint uppercase tracking-wide mb-3">Via the SMART Health IT launcher (recommended)</h2>
  <div class="<%= card_classes %>">
    <p class="text-sm text-muted mb-3 leading-relaxed">
      Works for both launch types — the launcher's "EHR Launch" mode redirects
      here with <code class="rounded bg-paper px-1 py-0.5 text-xs">iss</code> +
      <code class="rounded bg-paper px-1 py-0.5 text-xs">launch</code> set; its
      "Standalone Launch" mode redirects here with just <code class="rounded bg-paper px-1 py-0.5 text-xs">iss</code>,
      and <%= link_to "smart/launch", smart_ehr_launch_url, class: "text-accent underline underline-offset-2" %> detects which one it got and
      requests the right scope either way. Make sure you're signed in as a
      coordinator in this browser first, then:
    </p>
    <ol class="text-sm text-muted list-decimal list-inside space-y-1.5">
      <li>Go to <a href="https://launch.smarthealthit.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-accent underline underline-offset-2">launch.smarthealthit.org</a></li>
      <li>Set "App Launch URL" to <code class="rounded bg-paper px-1 py-0.5 text-xs"><%= smart_ehr_launch_url %></code></li>
      <li>Pick either launch type, configure a simulated patient, and click Launch</li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold text-faint uppercase tracking-wide mb-3">Bring your own iss</h2>
  <div class="<%= card_classes %>">
    <p class="text-sm text-muted mb-4 leading-relaxed">
      Initiates login ourselves against any FHIR server's SMART endpoints, no
      launcher round-trip needed — the authorization server prompts for a
      patient during login. Note: launch.smarthealthit.org's bare
      <code class="rounded bg-paper px-1 py-0.5 text-xs">/v/r4/fhir</code>
      endpoint rejects this (its authorize endpoint expects launch context
      minted via their launcher UI, even for "standalone") — this box is for a
      real EHR sandbox's SMART-enabled iss that supports launching without
      that round-trip.
    </p>

    <%= form_with url: smart_launch_path, method: :post, class: "flex gap-2" do |f| %>
      <%= f.text_field :iss, class: "#{input_classes} font-mono", placeholder: "FHIR server base URL (iss)" %>
      <%= f.submit "Connect via SMART on FHIR", class: "#{btn_primary} whitespace-nowrap" %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</section>
